   "parts": [
    [
     1,
     "Just found a link solve the problem, in case someone shall need it:<div><a href=\"http://neurochem.sisbio.recerca.upc.edu/?p=276\" target=\"_blank\" rel=\"nofollow\" data-saferedirecturl=\"https://www.google.com/url?hl=en-US&amp;q=http://neurochem.sisbio.recerca.upc.edu/?p%3D276&amp;source=gmail&amp;ust=1792407957569000&amp;usg=AOvVaw1mXLzIkZ0ZjyT1kD0xqbuR\">http://neurochem.sisbio.recerca.upc.edu/?p=276</a></div><div><br></div><div>With tiny modification on the code underneath:</div><div><br></div><div><span style=\"color:rgb(51,51,51);font-family:monospace;font-size:12px;line-height:19.1875px\">for(i in 1:nlevels(Y)) {</span><br style=\"color:rgb(51,51,51);font-family:monospace;font-size:12px;line-height:19.1875px\"><span style=\"color:rgb(51,51,51);font-family:monospace;font-size:12px;line-height:19.1875px\">y &lt;- levels(Y)[i]</span><br style=\"color:rgb(51,51,51);font-family:monospace;font-size:12px;line-height:19.1875px\"><span style=\"color:rgb(51,51,51);font-family:monospace;font-size:12px;line-height:19.1875px\">ind &lt;- which(Y == y)</span><br style=\"color:rgb(51,51,51);font-family:monospace;font-size:12px;line-height:19.1875px\"><span style=\"color:rgb(51,51,51);font-family:monospace;font-size:12px;line-height:19.1875px\">dat[ind, c(1, i+1)] &lt;- mod$x[ind, </span><span style=\"font-family:monospace;font-size:12px;line-height:19.1875px\"><font color=\"#ff0000\">pc</font></span><span style=\"color:rgb(51,51,51);font-family:monospace;font-size:12px;line-height:19.1875px\">]</span><br style=\"color:rgb(51,51,51);font-family:monospace;font-size:12px;line-height:19.1875px\"><span style=\"color:rgb(51,51,51);font-family:monospace;font-size:12px;line-height:19.1875px\">}</span></div><div><span style=\"color:rgb(51,51,51);font-family:monospace;font-size:12px;line-height:19.1875px\"><br></span></div><div><span style=\"color:rgb(51,51,51);font-family:monospace;font-size:12px;line-height:19.1875px\">should be:</span></div><div><span style=\"color:rgb(51,51,51);font-family:monospace;font-size:12px;line-height:19.1875px\">for(i in 1:nlevels(Y)) {</span><br style=\"color:rgb(51,51,51);font-family:monospace;font-size:12px;line-height:19.1875px\"><span style=\"color:rgb(51,51,51);font-family:monospace;font-size:12px;line-height:19.1875px\">y &lt;- levels(Y)[i]</span><br style=\"color:rgb(51,51,51);font-family:monospace;font-size:12px;line-height:19.1875px\"><span style=\"color:rgb(51,51,51);font-family:monospace;font-size:12px;line-height:19.1875px\">ind &lt;- which(Y == y)</span><br style=\"color:rgb(51,51,51);font-family:monospace;font-size:12px;line-height:19.1875px\"><span style=\"color:rgb(51,51,51);font-family:monospace;font-size:12px;line-height:19.1875px\">dat[ind, c(1, i+1)] &lt;- mod$x[ind, </span><span style=\"color:rgb(51,51,51);font-family:monospace;font-size:12px;line-height:19.1875px\">]</span><br style=\"color:rgb(51,51,51);font-family:monospace;font-size:12px;line-height:19.1875px\"><span style=\"color:rgb(51,51,51);font-family:monospace;font-size:12px;line-height:19.1875px\">}</span><span style=\"color:rgb(51,51,51);font-family:monospace;font-size:12px;line-height:19.1875px\"><br></span></div><div><span style=\"color:rgb(51,51,51);font-family:monospace;font-size:12px;line-height:19.1875px\"><br></span></div><div><span style=\"color:rgb(51,51,51);font-family:monospace;font-size:12px;line-height:19.1875px\">And I think package of &quot;pls&quot; is not in use.</span></div>"
    ],
    [
     3,
     "<div><span style=\"color:rgb(51,51,51);font-family:monospace;font-size:12px;line-height:19.1875px\"><br></span></div><div><br>On Wednesday, 17 July 2013 21:57:49 UTC+1, Joe Cheng [RStudio]  wrote:<blockquote class=\"gmail_quote\" style=\"margin:0;margin-left:0.8ex;border-left:1px #ccc solid;padding-left:1ex\"><div dir=\"ltr\">That&#39;s a good question for the googleVis guys, I don&#39;t think they monitor this list.</div><div><br><br><div class=\"gmail_quote\">On Wed, Jul 17, 2013 at 1:51 PM, xiong xiong <span dir=\"ltr\">&lt;<a rel=\"nofollow\">xxeri...@gmail.com</a>&gt;</span> wrote:<br>\r\n\r\n<blockquote class=\"gmail_quote\" style=\"margin:0 0 0 .8ex;border-left:1px #ccc solid;padding-left:1ex\">take Iris for example, how can I show different colours to different iris class on gvisScatterChart? since gvisScatterChart only take numerics, I would assign class some specific numbers, like &quot;<span style=\"line-height:18px\">Iris-setosa</span>&quot; = 1, but in visualisation part, don&#39;t get it....\r\n\r\n<span><font color=\"#888888\"><p></p>\r\n\r\n-- <br>\r\nYou received this message because you are subscribed to the Google Groups &quot;Shiny - Web Framework for R&quot; group.<br>\r\nTo unsubscribe from this group and stop receiving emails from it, send an email to <a rel=\"nofollow\">shiny-discus...@googlegroups.com</a>.<br>\r\nFor more options, visit <a href=\"https://groups.google.com/groups/opt_out\" target=\"_blank\" rel=\"nofollow\" data-saferedirecturl=\"https://www.google.com/url?hl=en-US&amp;q=https://groups.google.com/groups/opt_out&amp;source=gmail&amp;ust=1792407957569000&amp;usg=AOvVaw2sBeFcm5V-kc6-ypy9eZjg\">https://groups.google.com/groups/opt_out</a>.<br>\r\n <br>\r\n <br>\r\n</font></span></blockquote></div><br></div>\r\n</blockquote></div>"
